uildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', 'Other green creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nOther white creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Create Voja, a legendary 2/2 green and white Wolf creature token.', "Pack Rat's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Rats you control.\\n{2}{B}, Discard a card: Create a token that's a copy of Pack Rat.", "Players can't gain life this turn. Damage can't be prevented this turn. Skullcrack deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker.", "Populate. Creatures you control gain indestructible until end of turn. (To populate, create a token that's a copy of a creature token you control.)", 'Prime Speaker Zegana enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the greatest power among other creatures you control.\\nWhen Prime Speaker Zegana enters the battlefield, draw cards equal to its power.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature. That creature gains indestructible until end of turn.', "Put target attacking creature on the bottom of its owner's library. Its controller gains life equal to its toughness.", "Put target attacking or blocking creature on top of its owner's library.", "Put target creature with flying on the bottom of its owner's library.", "Put target nonland permanent on top of its owner's library.", 'Rakdos Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nEvolve (Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, if that creature has greater power or toughness than this creature, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)', 'Reach\\nWhen Arboreal Grazer enters the battlefield, you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.', "Replicate {1}{R} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nTarget Mountain becomes a 3/1 creature. It's still a land.", 'Replicate {R} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nDestroy target artifact.', 'Response deals 5 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', "Return all attacking creatures to their owner's hand.", 'Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "Return target nonland permanent with mana value X to its owner's hand.\\nDraw a card.", 'Return target nonland permanent you don\'t control to its owner\'s hand.\\nOverload {6}{U} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Return target permanent card from your graveyard to your hand. If a creature died this turn, create two 1/1 green Saproling creature tokens.', 'Return up to three target land cards from your graveyard to your hand.\\nDredge 3 (If you would draw a card, you may mill three cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand, then discard a card.', 'Return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Reveal a card from your hand. Search your library for a card with the same name as that card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\nHellbent — If you have no cards in hand, instead search your library for a card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Riot (This creature enters the battlefield with your choice of a +1/+1 counter or haste.)', 'Riot (This creature enters the battlefield with your choice of a +1/+1 counter or haste.)\\nWhenever Burning-Tree Vandal attacks, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.', 'Sacrifice Keening Apparition: Destroy target enchantment.', 'Sacrifice Shambling Shell: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nDredge 3 (If you would draw a card, you may mill three cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Sacrifice another creature: Cartel Aristocrat gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice three white creatures: Exile target creature.\\nWhenever another black creature you control dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', "Scavenge {0} ({0}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", "Scavenge {5}{G} ({5}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", 'Search your library for a Plains, Island, Swamp, or Mountain card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card or Gate card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Selesnya Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', 'Simic Guildgate enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Spectacle {2}{B} (You may cast this spell for its spectacle cost rather than its mana cost if an opponent lost life this turn.)\\nWhen Blade Juggler enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to you and you draw a card.', 'Spectacle {R} (You may cast this spell for its spectacle cost rather than its mana cost if an opponent lost life this turn.)\\nExile the top two cards of your library. Until the end of your next turn, you may play those cards.', 'Spectacle {R} (You may cast this spell for its spectacle cost rather than its mana cost if an opponent lost life this turn.)\\nSkewer the Critics deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Summary Judgment deals 3 damage to target tapped creature.\\nAddendum — If you cast this spell during your main phase, it deals 5 damage instead.', "Sunder Shaman can't be blocked by more than one creature.\\nWhenever Sunder Shaman deals combat damage to a player, destroy target artifact or enchantment that player controls.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\nScavenge {2}{B} ({2}{B}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", 'Target creature gains deathtouch until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\nAddendum — If you cast this spell during your main phase, that creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/-3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nDredge 3 (If you would draw a card, you may mill three cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Target creature gets -3/-3 until end of turn.', "Target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to target creature or planeswalker you don't control.", 'Target creature you don\'t control gets -4/-0 until end of turn.\\nOverload {2}{U} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target opponent sacrifices a creature. If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, you gain 4 life.', 'Target player draws three cards. Then that player discards two cards unless they discard a land card.', 'The next 1 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn is dealt to another target creature instead.\\nDraw a card.', 'The next sorcery spell you cast this turn can be cast as though it had flash. (It can be cast any time you could cast an instant.)\\nDraw a card.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy all creatures.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nFlying\\nWhenever you draw a card, Niv-Mizzet, Parun deals 1 damage to any target.\\nWhenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell, you draw a card.", "This spell costs {1} less to cast for each Gate you control.\\nGate Colossus can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or less.\\nWhenever a Gate enters the battlefield under your control, you may put Gate Colossus from your graveyard on top of your library.", "This spell costs {1} less to cast if it targets a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nTarget creature you control fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", "Trample\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Trample\\nWhenever Borborygmos Enraged deals combat damage to a player, reveal the top three cards of your library. Put all land cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\nDiscard a land card: Borborygmos Enraged deals 3 damage to any target.', "Trample\\nWhenever Ilharg, the Raze-Boar attacks, you may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped and attacking. Return that creature to your hand at the beginning of the next end step.\\nWhen Ilharg, the Raze-Boar dies or is put into exile from the battlefield, you may put it into its owner's library third from the top.", "Trample\\nWhenever Mindleech Mass deals combat damage to a player, you may look at that player's hand. If you do, you may cast a spell from among those cards without paying its mana cost.", 'Untap all creatures you control.\\nDraw a card.', 'Up to two target creatures you control each deal damage equal to their power to another target creature.', 'Vigilance', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Conclave Cavalier dies, create two 2/2 green and white Elf Knight creature tokens with vigilance.', "When Azorius Arrester enters the battlefield, detain target creature an opponent controls. (Until your next turn, that creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated.)", "When Azorius Justiciar enters the battlefield, detain up to two target creatures your opponents control. (Until your next turn, those creatures can't attack or block and their activated abilities can't be activated.)", 'When Bulwark Giant enters the battlefield, you gain 5 life.', 'When Burglar Rat enters the battlefield, each opponent discards a card.', "When Coiling Oracle enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a land card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put that card into your hand.", "When Fblthp, the Lost enters the battlefield, draw a card. If it entered from your library or was cast from your library, draw two cards instead.\\nWhen Fblthp becomes the target of a spell, shuffle Fblthp into its owner's library.", 'When Footlight Fiend dies, it deals 1 damage to any target.', 'When Glowspore Shaman enters the battlefield, mill three cards. You may put a land card from your graveyard on top of your library. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', 'When Golgari Findbroker enters the battlefield, return target permanent card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Golgari Thug dies, put target creature card from your graveyard on top of your library.\\nDredge 4 (If you would draw a card, you may mill four cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', "When Kiora's Dambreaker enters the battlefield, proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)", "When Lazav, the Multifarious enters the battlefield, surveil 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put it into your graveyard.)\\n{X}: Lazav, the Multifarious becomes a copy of target creature card in your graveyard with mana value X, except its name is Lazav, the Multifarious, it's legendary in addition to its other types, and it has this ability.", 'When Loaming Shaman enters the battlefield, target player shuffles any number of target cards from their graveyard into their library.', "When Mausoleum Turnkey enters the battlefield, return target creature card of an opponent's choice from your graveyard to your hand.", "When Mortus Strider dies, return it to its owner's hand.", "When Plaguecrafter enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices a creature or planeswalker. Each player who can't discards a card.", 'When Protean Hulk dies, search your library for any number of creature cards with total mana value 6 or less, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'When Rakdos Firewheeler enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to target opponent and 2 damage to up to one target creature or planeswalker.', 'When Rest in Peace enters the battlefield, exile all graveyards.\\nIf a card or token would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.', 'When Urbis Protector enters the battlefield, create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying.', "Whenever Aetherplasm blocks a creature, you may return Aetherplasm to its owner's hand. If you do, you may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield blocking that creature.", 'Whenever Vedalken Mesmerist attacks, target creature an opponent controls gets -2/-0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, it gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of creatures you control.', 'Whenever a creature you control dies, draw a card.\\n[+1]: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\n[−4]: Each player sacrifices two creatures.\\n[−9]: Each opponent chooses a permanent they control of each permanent type and sacrifices the rest.', "Whenever a nonartifact permanent enters the battlefield under your control, you may return another permanent you control that shares a permanent type with it to its owner's hand.", "Whenever a nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, if it doesn't have the same name as another creature you control or a creature card in your graveyard, draw a card.", 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, Midnight Reaper deals 1 damage to you and you draw a card.', 'Whenever a player sacrifices a permanent, Mayhem Devil deals 1 damage to any target.', "Whenever an ability of equipped creature is activated, if it isn't a mana ability, copy that ability. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\nEquip {3}", "Whenever an opponent casts a noncreature spell, Cindervines deals 1 damage to that player.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Cindervines: Destroy target artifact or enchantment. Cindervines deals 2 damage to that permanent's controller.", "Whenever another black creature enters the battlefield under your control, target creature gains intimidate until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", 'Whenever another creature or planeswalker you control dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Rising Populace.', 'Whenever another creature you control dies, Vindictive Vampire deals 1 damage to each opponent and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, Burning Prophet gets +1/+0 until end of turn, then scry 1.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Guttersnipe deals 2 damage to each opponent.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 blue Bird Illusion creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you gain life, put two +1/+1 counters on Karlov of the Ghost Council.\\n{W}{B}, Remove six +1/+1 counters from Karlov of the Ghost Council: Exile target creature.', 'Whenever you sacrifice a black creature, you may pay 2 life. If you do, each other player sacrifices a creature.\\nWhenever you sacrifice a green creature, you may gain 2 life.', "You can't cast this spell unless an opponent lost life this turn.\\nFlying, trample\\nCreature spells you cast cost {1} less to cast for each 1 life your opponents have lost this turn.", 'You gain X life and draw X cards.', 'You may have Copy Enchantment enter the battlefield as a copy of any enchantment on the battlefield.', 'You may have Gigantoplasm enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has "{X}: This creature has base power and toughness X/X."', "You may have Spark Double enter the battlefield as a copy of a creature or planeswalker you control, except it enters with an additional +1/+1 counter on it if it's a creature, it enters with an additional loyalty counter on it if it's a planeswalker, and it isn't legendary.", '[+1]: Exile up to two target cards from a single graveyard. You gain 2 life if at least one creature card was exiled this way.\\n[−1]: Exile target nonland permanent with mana value 1 or less.\\n[−5]: Kaya, Orzhov Usurper deals damage to target player equal to the number of cards that player owns in exile and you gain that much life.', '[+1]: Look at the top card of your library. If it\'s a creature card, you may reveal it and put it into your hand.\\n[−2]: Target creature you control fights another target creature.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "Creatures you control have double strike, trample, hexproof, and haste."', '[+1]: Tap target permanent, then untap another target permanent.\\n[−2]: Ral Zarek deals 3 damage to any target.\\n[−7]: Flip five coins. Take an extra turn after this one for each coin that comes up heads.', '{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Search your library for a land card with a basic land type, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{1}, {T}, Tap an untapped creature you control: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Target player mills a card. (They put the top card of their library into their graveyard.)\\nTap four untapped Advisors you control: Target player mills twelve cards.\\nA deck can have any number of cards named Persistent Petitioners.', '{1}, {T}: Untap target creature that has an activated ability with {T} in its cost.', '{1}{R}: Greater Forgeling gets +3/-3 until end of turn.', '{1}{R}: Target creature gains haste until end of turn.\\n{1}{W}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.', "{2}, Sacrifice Voyager Staff: Exile target creature. Return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", "{2}{G}{U}: Adapt 1. (If this creature has no +1/+1 counters on it, put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhenever one or more +1/+1 counters are put on Sharktocrab, tap target creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "{2}{W}: Tap target creature.\\n{2}{U}: Counter target activated ability. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)", '{2}{W}: Target player gains 1 life.\\n{2}{B}: Each player loses 1 life.', '{3}{G}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.\\n{3}{W}: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Silent Dart: It deals 3 damage to target creature.', '{4}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n{4}{G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', '{R}, Sacrifice a creature: Scorched Rusalka deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', '{R}{R}: Rakdos Pit Dragon gains flying until end of turn.\\n{R}: Rakdos Pit Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nHellbent — Rakdos Pit Dragon has double strike as long as you have no cards in hand.', '{T}, Sacrifice two other creatures: Any number of target players each lose 2 life and sacrifice a creature. You add {B}{B} and draw a card.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Thespian's Stage becomes a copy of target land, except it has this ability.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', '{T}: Create X 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens, where X is the number of Goblins you control.', '{T}: Exile target land card from a graveyard. Add one mana of any color.\\n{B}, {T}: Exile target instant or sorcery card from a graveyard. Each opponent loses 2 life.\\n{G}, {T}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. You gain 2 life.']
flavor: ['". . . and furthermore . . ."', '"About the sphinx, I have mixed feelings. Their wisdom I crave, but their secrecy I can\'t tolerate."\\n—Szadek', '"All dead move to the hollow rhythm of necromancy."\\n—Savra', '"All matter, animate or not, rots when exposed to time. We merely speed up the process."\\n—Ezoc, Golgari rot farmer', '"Allow me a moment to catch your breath."', '"Before I let you wield one of these, let\'s see you dodge one!"', '"By all means, take another step toward the captain."', '"By the time your knees have worn through your robe, you may have begun to learn your place."', '"Does Teysa think me blind to her scheming? Ambition runs in our family."', '"Even rats hoard their treasures. Are your precious things so different?"\\n—Izoni', '"Everyone deserves a day in court."', '"First, you must fight among the rank and file. It is there I will discern your skills as a leader."\\n—Aurelia, to Gideon Jura', '"For every inch of land they take from us, we take it back or we burn it. Give them nothing."\\n—Aurelia', '"Four parts molten bronze, yes . . . one part frozen mercury, yes, yes . . . but then what?"', '"Four parts molten bronze, yes ... one part frozen mercury, yes, yes ... but then what?"', '"From a great bonfire at the dawn of time, the first Gruul kindled their rage. The same flame burns in you."\\n—Kroshkar, Gruul shaman', '"Have you ever held a Boros signet? There\'s a weight to it that belies its size—a weight of strength and of pride."\\n—Agrus Kos', '"He displays a perverse charisma fueled by avarice. Highly dangerous. Recommend civil sanctions."\\n—Agmand Sarv, Azorius hussar', '"Hold on to your ideals. They\'ll be tested more than your armor or the edge of your blade."\\n—Tajic', '"Hop away now, little Eternal. Go eat some flies."\\n—Kasmina', '"How truly vast this city must be, that I have traveled so far and seen so much, yet never once found the place where the buildings fail."', '"I appreciate things that exceed expectations."\\n—Mizzix', '"I can call an army to my side in the blink of an eye. Best not blink."', '"I can\'t protect everyone here. But those I can, I will."\\n—Karn', '"I do not know which gives me more pride: the legions of soldiers marching in thunderous lockstep, or the cry of the skyknights riding their rocs like jagged lightning overhead."\\n—Razia', '"I hear that Boros is losing its angels to the Gateless Movement. I\'m sure this comes as no surprise to you."\\n—Teysa, to Lazav', '"I see countless worlds. What makes them think I can\'t find them in just one?"\\n—Ral Zarek', '"I told Jace that Ravnica would fall apart if he didn\'t take his responsibilities seriously. I didn\'t want to be right."', '"I watched its blade swing through me, but I was hollow, empty. I saw its face contort in rage but could not hear it snarl."\\n—Klattic, Boros legionnaire', '"I\'d rather see the guilds contend together with words in the halls of power, than in the streets with swords."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"If we cannot have peace, we will have justice."\\n—Aurelia', '"If you don\'t have a destination in mind, the route is all that matters."\\n—Tamina, district guide', '"It is technically an ooze, but its lifespan measures only seconds. In that short time, its appetite for magic is extraordinary."\\n—Simic research notes', '"It makes better use of Uncle Dragi\'s head than he ever did."\\n—Pesha, retired blacksmith', '"It misses nothing and it has no sense of humor."\\n—Barvisa, courtroom scribe', '"Just as leaves fall and the tree blooms again, one day I will fall and the Conclave will endure."', '"Law is the light of civilization."', '"Let him be an example to others who would default on their debts to us."\\n—"The Cozen," Orzhov assassin', '"Let the knowledge of absolute law inspire you to live a life of absolute order."', '"Let the song of Selesnya be heard above the rhythm of our thundering hordes!"', '"Look at this creature, so like the Conclave it serves. Cut one head and it grows two. Damage it and it flourishes."\\n—Veszka, Selesnya evangel', '"Many wings haunt the skies these days. Few of them bear good tidings."\\n—Lavinia', '"Meat *and* eggs. We eat!"\\n—Borborygmos', '"Most compete for insects at street level. Some dwell near Izzet laboratories and ride the thermal updrafts."\\n—Yolov, Simic bioengineer', '"My greatest creation—me!"', '"My power is generosity, in a way. I give my survivors an appreciation for their lives."', '"Nature\'s most raw beauty is the circle: perfect in its continuance, with no break between death and life."', '"No doubt the arbiters would put you away, after all the documents are signed. But I will have justice now."\\n—Alovnek, Boros guildmage', '"No harm can come to me while the Worldsoul shelters me."', '"None may pass . . . for free."', '"Places, everyone!"\\n—Judith', '"Selesnya\'s soil is sacred, and you\'re about to meet it with your face."', '"Some bend the law. I tie it into knots."', '"Subtlety is for lawmages and spies."', '"That giant didn\'t even see me, let alone catch me! And I was close enough to smell him! Of course, that\'s not saying much."', '"The Gruul embrace all things poisonous and living in the cracks of society."\\n—Teysa Karlov', '"The Selesnya are gathering armies. Do you still believe they aren\'t preparing for war?"\\n—Teysa, to Isperia', '"The call came, spell-borne through mortar and stone to the ear of every soldier. The call came, and the advantage was ours."\\n—Lodusz, captain of the watch', '"The clamor of the city drowns all voices. But together we can sing a harmony that will resonate from Ravnica\'s tallest spires to her deepest wells."', '"The maaka remain loyal to us in this time of strife. We don\'t even have to feed them—our enemies do."\\n—Nedja, Gruul shaman', '"The pain of searing iron and razor edges pales beside the pleasure of performance."\\n—Judith', '"The suffering of others is not my concern."', '"There\'s no need to sound the alarm. You are minding your post admirably. I am authorized. All is well."', '"These terms are acceptable to House Dimir. Shall we shake on it?"', '"They\'ve got eyes inside my head!"', '"This day will end in death, but not the one you hoped for. This day will end in victory, but not the one you expected."', '"This footlight\'s broken. Get me a stagehand!"\\n—Judith', '"This one opens the grate outside Zelzo Base. This one is for Ismeri Library. This one is for an invisible door . . . No, I\'ve said too much."', '"Three daggers left in an angel\'s back, three enforcers with memory loss, three keys stolen from my own belt—and you talk of peace?"\\n—Tajic, to Aurelia', '"Through the haze of battle I saw the glint of sun on golden mane, the sheen of glory clad in mail, and I dropped my sword and wept at the idiocy of war."\\n—Dravin, Gruul deserter', '"Touched by moroii"\\n—Undercity slang meaning "to grow old"', '"Walls crack. Buildings fall. Always the wilds return."\\n—Domri Rade', '"We fight to stop a tyrant, but we also fight for the gentle creatures who have no concept of what befalls their world."\\n—Vivien Reid', '"We gather the past from surface dwellers and sell it right back to them."', '"We have intel that some guilds have fallen under an invader\'s influence. Until we\'re sure, no venture succeeds."\\n—Lazav', '"We\'re all food for something in the end."\\n—Cevraya, Golgari shaman', '"We\'re on the fortieth floor, with one window, no balcony. No one could possibly get in."\\n—Minosz, Orzhov chief of security', '"We\'re planting the seeds of change. Sometimes, we plant them in people."\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"Well, at least all of that arm-waving and arcane babbling you did was impressive."', '"What bait do you cast to catch a dream?"\\n—Ravnican riddle', '"What root and branch cannot reach, our winged friends will attend to."\\n—Zunak, Selesnya strategist', '"When properly invoked, the plasma globule encloses the offensive spell with a satisfying slurp."', '"When your enemy flees, send the sea to pursue them."\\n—Kiora', '"Where did *she* come from? More importantly, are there more like her?"\\n—Gideon Jura', '"You can come back once you\'ve learned some manners—and figured out how to reconstitute your physical forms."', '"You have the right to remain silent. Mostly because I tire of your excuses."', '"You take our wilds, we take your city."', '"You\'ll pay what you owe, with your money or your life."', '"You\'re right. I\'m sure your Legion friends *are* looking for you. And once we\'ve hidden a piece of you in each district, they\'ll get to keep looking for a long time."\\n—Ivrelya, Dimir spymaster', '"Your arrival was expected...and unwelcome."', '"Your deed cannot be undone. You, however, can be."\\n—Agosto, Azorius imperator', '"Your life serves a higher purpose now: ensuring the continuation of my own."', '"Your potential to commit a crime warrants further investigation."', 'A skilled Izzet chronarch can carry out an epic vendetta between the fall of one hourglass grain and the next.', 'Amid rumors of war, the third act of The *Absolution of the Guildpact* was quickly rewritten as a tragedy.', 'An emblem of a secret guild, the Dimir insignia is seen only by its own members—and the doomed.', 'Any challenge to Azorius authority is met with swift and potent retribution.', 'As brilliant as a cut diamond, and with just as cruel an edge.', 'As the bounty on Massacre Girl rose, so did the number of imitators.', 'Azorius sphinxes are loyal to the precepts of the law, not to any particular guildmaster—even one of their own kind.', "By design, the sarcophagus muffles the debtors' moans but does not silence them.", 'Centaurs are sent to evangelize in Gruul territories where words of war speak louder than prayers of peace.', 'Depending on your point of view, the seal represents a proud guardian of the natural cycle or one who has sold her soul to darkness for eternal life.', "Despite their stake in the city's survival, Rakdos cultists are loath to pass up any opportunity to sow chaos.", 'Dimir mages put the lanterns to good use, creating shapeshifters and sleeper agents from mana foreign to them.', "Dimir's best agents hide from death itself.", 'During their ascent to spirithood, patriarchs of Orzhova shed both flesh and emotion. This earthly slag is collected and formed into thrulls.', 'Each small blaze she sets jogs her memory, letting her piece together the mystery of her own fiery end.', 'Each soul he devours adds its hunger to his own.', 'Enter and become a mastermind of spies, lies, and deception.', 'Enter and comprehend the perfection of orchestrated life.', 'Enter and indulge your darkest fantasies, for you may never pass this way again.', 'Enter and leave the shackles of society behind.', 'Enter and rejoice! The Conclave stands united, open to one and all.', 'Enter the Senate, the seat of justice and the foundation of Ravnican society.', 'Enter those who are starving and sick. You are welcome among the Swarm when the rest of Ravnica rejects you.', 'Enter those with the vision to create and the daring to release their creations.', 'Enter to find wealth, security, and eternal life . . . for just a small price up front.', 'Enter with merciful hearts. Exit with battle cries.', 'Equenauts are the seeds of the Conclave, scattered on the four winds, searching for new places to take root.', 'Ever wonder why you never see an old Rakdos cultist?', 'Fblthp had always hated crowds.', "Few have seen the inner workings of Ravnica's furnaces, but neighboring districts catch brief glimpses in the horrors that escape the flames.", 'For the Simic Combine, its sigil serves not as an emblem of honor but as a trademark. Its familiar image on any biological commodity attests to superb craftsmanship, ingenious innovation, and higher cost.', 'From death she grows living grandeur.', "Genius is finding the edge of what's possible, then jumping over it.", 'Going to a Rakdos show is dangerous. Trying to leave early can be fatal.', 'Greatness, at any cost.', 'Grief is a crucible where resolve is tempered.', 'Gruul territorial markings need not be legible. The blood, snot, and muck used to smear them are unmistakably Gruul.', "He has a job to finish, and it's you.", 'He unmakes the world in his own image.', 'He wants to watch Ravnica burn, one soul at a time.', "Her enemy's strength is her own.", 'His work determines who is remembered and who feeds the worms.', 'In Rakdos-controlled neighborhoods, everyone is part of the show.', 'In theory, the Guildpact keeps guild feuds from spiraling out of control. Personal feuds, however, are not covered.', 'In times of peril, the vision the ancient paruns had for their city comes into focus.', 'Into the light the good are welcomed, and with the light the evil are banished.', 'It *wants* to remain a mystery, banishing the curious in favor of less inquisitive company.', "It departs through the streets' fissures with a sound like gravel pouring into a pond.", "It's easy to believe you're a god when you're twice as powerful as everyone else.", 'Its fickle form holds hints of a thousand former identities.', "Krenko's hirelings are unflinchingly loyal.", "Leonos had no second thoughts about the abolishment edict. He'd left skyrunes warning of the eviction, even though it was cloudy.", "Long ago, birds of paradise littered the skies. Thanks to the city's sprawl, most now exist as pets of society's elite.", "Lyzolda's pet rats eat better than the average citizen. In fact, they can usually be found eating the average citizen.", 'Made of bone and boiled in blood, a Rakdos signet is not considered finished until it has been used as a murder weapon.', "Man's best fungus.", 'No one welcomes his visit, yet all must grant him tribute.', "One man's trash is another man's troller.", 'Quyzl was told by his mentor to "make more time" for his studies.', "Ravnica's safest strongholds are often neither.", 'Rumors float through the city like crows, alighting on citizens seemingly at random.', 'Saprolings add the three and the four to the "one-two punch."', 'Scream: muffled. Pockets: emptied. Neck function: never the same again.', 'Seen through Rakdos eyes, a cruel betrayal is a hilarious stunt.', 'Simic mages create redundant backups of their experiments to reduce the consequences of catastrophe.', "Simic's strength comes from its diversity.", 'Snaking remnants of nature directed by a body of thought and progress, the oracles embody all that is Simic.', 'Some corpses the Golgari cannot claim. Some souls the Orzhov cannot shackle.', "Some of Orzhov's cruelest collectors remember their debtors by taste alone.", 'Some sky steeds break from the thundering herd to ride free on the open winds.', 'Some souls are too damaged to be of use to the Orzhov.', 'Some storms never blow over.', 'Some use magic to spy through walls. Others use it to crush them.', "Some view Domri's unlikely ascent as a sign of Ilharg the Raze-Boar's imminent return.", 'Something roams the killing places, sniffing the guilt of the slayers, stalking them on iron paws.', 'Street folk call them "spire mice," but behind the mockery is an unspoken envy of the ledgewalkers\' skill at avoiding harm.', "Suddenly, all the haggling didn't seem so important.", 'The Dimir agents watched from the shadows. "Eight hours, and I\'ve yet to see him blink," Nefara hissed. "I suggest we find another way in."', 'The Izzet signet is redesigned often, each time becoming closer to a vanity portrait of Niv-Mizzet.', 'The Izzet specialize in unnatural disaster.', 'The Orzhov are not the only religious tradition on Ravnica, nor the oldest.', 'The Rakdos believe that all are eager to join their revels, even when told otherwise.', "The Street Swarm is the labor class that drives the Golgari's endless cycle of life and death.", 'The druid knew only one spell, a charm to encourage rapid plant growth. When airborne Eternals invaded her arboretum, she had to get creative.', 'The fear of dragons is as old and as powerful as the fear of death itself.', 'The fearful want the procedure before a blood festival. The guilty seek it afterward.', "The feline Eternal felt Liliana's command, looked at her disdainfully, flicked its paw, and scampered away across the rooftops.", "The lawmage's argument was clever and well reasoned, but Blunk's response proved irrefutable.", 'The maze-like design embodies the core of Azorius law—strict structure designed to test wills and stall change.', 'The ostentatious splendor of the Orzhov church was just asking to be smashed.', 'The sigil holds different meanings depending on its form and presentation. While some wear it as a sign of status, others wear it as a sign of debt.', 'The star performer of the Juri Revue, his shows have fans and blood spilling into the street.', 'The stones hark back to an age before civilization, when the living earth blessed all who trod its untamed wilds.', 'The symbol of the Conclave is one of unity, with tree supporting sun and sun feeding tree.', 'The taste of blood breaks down what little self-control the Rakdos possess.', 'The undercity is always hungry.', "Their ranks are thin, their formation is improvised, their weapons are borrowed, and you'd best get out of their way.", 'There is no knowledge that is not power.', "They are the voice of the wild, crying out with nature's fury and bringing forth its primeval might.", 'They inflict pain to forget their own and break foes to feel whole.', 'Those without a guild signet often display a different form of protection.', "Though less well-known than its army of soldiers, the Boros Legion's mage-priests are as respected by the innocent as they are hated by the ghosts of the guilty.", 'To bear the shield of the pariah is the highest honor a Boros can receive—and the last.', 'Tumult is its natural habitat.', 'Voyager staffs are sought by those hoping to find an escape from the sprawling glut of Ravnica.', 'When asked how much power is required, Izzet mages always answer "more."', 'When giant sinkholes opened across Ravnica, they revealed buried oceans and the merfolk, once thought to be extinct.', 'When he reaches for his key ring, you should be running for the exit.', 'When the price of your sins comes due, the Church of Deals is there to collect.', 'Whoever wins, the neighborhood loses.']
